group: C2v
formula: NO2
construction: a central atom and its neighbours
headline: 
note: Fragments: a central atom and its neighbours · energies in Hartree · labels in C<sub>2v</sub> · 3 core orbitals hidden
about: **What is drawn.** The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree. This is an unrestricted calculation: the levels are drawn at their alpha energies, and the beta electrons are matched to them by symmetry.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in C2v; the code reported none.\n\n**The circles beside each symmetry orbital** show the atoms as seen from one side, filled and open for opposite sign and sized by weight; a bar is a p lobe in the page.\n\n**Not shown.** 3 core orbitals below −14.23 Hartree.
